<title>USA: NYSE Unavailables - Tosco, Airborne Freight, American Stores, Medtronic and Times Mirror.</title>
<headline>NYSE Unavailables - Tosco, Airborne Freight, American Stores, Medtronic and Times Mirror.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Monday that Tosco Corp, Airborne Freight Corp, American Stores Co, Medtronic Inc and Times Mirror Co were not available for after-hours trading for news.  </p>
<p>Earlier in the day, Tosco said it would do a three-for-one stock split, Airborne and American Stores released their fourth-quarter earnings, Medtronic had one of its devices cleared by the government, while the Times Mirror was considering the sale of all or part of its Tejon stake.</p>
<p>The exchange said Public Service Enterprise Group Inc, Corimon SACA, Westmoreland Coal Co and Westmoreland preferred A stock were also unavailable.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
